ingine-batch
Copyright 2026 satellitedown

This repository contains ingine (a C++/CUDA inference engine for
Inkling-2-Mini, in native/) with batched serving of many concurrent requests,
and benchmark tools (bench/). All of it is licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0 (see LICENSE), except the vendored dependencies listed below,
which keep their own licenses.

It is a fork of the ingine in
https://github.com/satellitedown/inkling-2-mini-abliterated-ingine
(Apache License 2.0, commit 556acc7), without that repository's abliteration
tools, abliteration file and installer.

The model weights are not part of this repository. This license does not
replace the licenses of downloaded software or model artifacts.

ingine's C++ engine
-------------------
Its device, memory, weight-loading, CUDA-graph and tracing infrastructure, the
OpenAI-compatible HTTP server and the tokenizer and chat-template pipeline are
adapted from fngine (Apache License 2.0):
https://github.com/satellitedown/fngine
fngine is derived in part from Cinference (commit 383e5db,
https://github.com/satellitedown/cinference), which is derived from NInfer by
Neroued and its contributors (https://github.com/Neroued/ninfer), all under
the Apache License, Version 2.0. Adapted files carry a header of the form
"Adapted from fngine (github.com/satellitedown/fngine, Apache-2.0) for
ingine.", and files fngine took from Cinference keep their "Modified for
fngine from cinference:<path> @ 383e5db. See NOTICE." header. The model
kernels, the prefill, the DSpark drafter, the speculative decoding loop and the
batched decoding, drafting and scheduling are written for Inkling-2-Mini; the
decode kernels are ports of ingine's earlier PyTorch extension kernels.

